{
  "family": "doublebox2m",
  "source": "Doublebox 2L 4-leg with interleaved 2-mass scheme — mAsq on l1 prop 0 AND l2 prop 3; mBsq on l1 prop 1 AND l2 prop 5.  Cross-loop mass placement gives the top-sector differential-equation matrix a complex-conjugate pole pair at eta = -1/2 +- i sqrt(47)/2 (|eta| approx 3.46), which tightens the Frobenius series convergence radius for the 4 top-sector masters relative to single-mass / block-mass schemes.  C++ therefore needs roughly doubled x_order and extra_x_order to produce the correct value (working_pre=200, x_order=400, extra_x_order=480 succeeds; the original defaults working_pre=160, x_order=200, extra_x_order=240 produced a sign-flipped Re and O(0.1) spurious Im).  Regression guard for D12 — see docs/AUDIT_MMA_PARITY.md.",
